ath. And hearing this, O descendant or Raghu, do you settle what you think proper.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.662,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-74-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7065008","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1cd218c3226a77e218657af3d00b5b856c4f33eafd26d516b77f95192a7c015d","compact":"e7f95d2a30764cf1d0682cb96eb93c7804a2c9dda667d03dcf1ff3a252213bff","nasal":"47ff44f965a7bdd62e7b9c5f04153609d2a9815c8de0dfccf0fca61e7fc93b76"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-65-9","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":65,"verse":9,"english":"O king, in the golden age, only the Brahmanas used to engage in asceticism. At that age save the Brāhmaṇas no other caste used to lead the life of an anchoret.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.86,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-74-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7065009","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"450f60ee4a6176ac425153a959f865c47e07790ea498022a51bd2c159c057fea","compact":"c2b3f03ddd8fc0ccd5d8e95e7daf0a839af599e3d392b04ea7e8f4ee4b817470","nasal":"ac875db0ba921b68f45d34464e8b585bbc6f5a6a8ec206dca3cc48848c6d7714"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-65-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":65,"verse":10,"english":"And for this, the Brāhmaṇas were the highest caste, effulgent in asceticism, asceticism, shorn shorn of ignorance, above death and conversant with three ages.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-74-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7065010","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c70671040eca5ffdddc5d7b3751d682f6bcac8c7050c00527cb35a47c9315504","compact":"6c17e07a9011ee708dde657fe1cc18afe06e4c98c6faf30b0f9236bf07cbbce8","nasal":"6c17e07a9011ee708dde657fe1cc18afe06e4c98c6faf30b0f9236bf07cbbce8"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-65-11","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":65,"verse":11,"english":"There upon at the end of the golden age, Brāhmaṇa's understanding became loose and the Tretā Yuga set in. At this age Kşatriyas, gifted with the power acquired by pristine asceticism, were born. And those men, intent upon austere penances, that were born in the Tretā age, were more powerful and greater devotees than those in the former age.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-74-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7065011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f76b39f916cd5bd15a24c120490a5f91a531fa623d386b318543d79f7808f94a","compact":"a4f8b743add6e35957d1898c3cd5674cadbb64dc921083e412591b2744ba3bb4","nasal":"a777ab48e9a9c32b90f6f8b2a5e09624afd3f0dc133c683969fe9ca4b52b3a11"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-65-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":65,"verse":12,"english":"There upon at the end of the golden age, Brāhmaṇa's understanding became loose and the Tretā Yuga set in. At this age Kşatriyas, gifted with the power acquired by pristine asceticism, were born. And those men, intent upon austere penances, that were born in the Tretā age, were more powerful and greater devotees than those in the former age.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.844,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-74-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7065012","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ed88219ee3df5092ae039ca566b4dd22aae8afb126bd1b7485a862b2ebac2f63","compact":"bea2e7e9d1741a3b77735da4f594aadb3dcc079ab5866b945e257b5583e4610c","nasal":"bea2e7e9d1741a3b77735da4f594aadb3dcc079ab5866b945e257b5583e4610c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-65-13","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":65,"verse":13,"english":"In the golden age the Brāhmaṇas were more powerful than the Kșatriyas. But in the Tretā age the Brāhmaṇas and the Ksatriyas were equally powerful.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.734,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-74-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7065013","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c84c5a538da3c9115cb4a2f0d4c158a27a7de735bdd6e4e9d9d3249456333e33","compact":"6c5b6df4a75928b51cb287f3ffbc3561161e56660be12940b41d3054b96500b0","nasal":"6c5b6df4a75928b51cb287f3ffbc3561161e56660be12940b41d3054b96500b0"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-65-14","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":65,"verse":14,"english":"Thus in the Tretā age, not beholding prominence of the Brāhmaṇas greater than that of the Kşatriyas, Manu and other religious leaders of the time composed the Sastra describing and setting in the four divisions of castes.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.922,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-74-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7065014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3bba7d53e81544fa066f61aee166e27e525da4c2bef1c4df9ac0de766a92de2e","compact":"de58b71a6438dde166a5b3f372e1edab0dab5873a4ba87ff9a38a21a057abbbe","nasal":"88d7d35d825a2845c8771f5fca5145d8cfc6f7233148d869ed5f085073dd5870"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-65-15","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":65,"verse":15,"english":"In this wise the Tretā age was prolific with virtues of the four Varņas, and many pious sacrifices and was shorn of iniquities. But being attacked a little with iniquity, one portion of sin appeared on earth. And growing impious people of sin appeared on earth. And growing impious people lost their strength.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.639,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-74-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7065015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f751ae1ed0eea64c8c6a7eef1e77b11c8909903418dcc74a862209090baf5bc8","compact":"1f4d8ddc8c5b7353b5f1c3833a7e272726a3df266fed3749bc0c3f5ffd9dd4c1","nasal":"84315338172874bc1cbb0e800883a41e125f495a75558c1001cba6dfa99eee68"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-65-16","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":65,"verse":16,"english":"And for houses and farms that were the property of the former age, people of the Tretā Yuga were possessed by envy, the outcome of the quality of darkness. And with the treading of impiety on earth during Tretā, the soiled sin of untruth appeared. And this iniquity stretching one footstep, the lease of people's lives, for sins, became limited.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.47,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-74-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7065016","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"df911ab5251d6aabe32ee1b92bba623f6bdab039b1561371be4365344965f089","compact":"322800093149aba793475da739804a92ee840d6a7614efcc40418f37268c341f","nasal":"322800093149aba793475da739804a92ee840d6a7614efcc40418f37268c341f"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-65-17","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":65,"verse":17,"english":"During the Tretă age the Brāhmaṇas and Kș atriyas engaged in austere penances and the Vaiśyas and Sūdras engaged in serving them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.652,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-74-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7065017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7753a94710245ace88d93fdf3af9391662af7c041f60b0e52ccf76f037975ae5","compact":"f25e9d1714b37ac8b7e9a3451b87ea1f9b03f2f45d456fcd69fbf113ec54422a","nasal":"6604eed3f49ae2434552b2327c75487201723cc4f4e603613429a4f6387d9a9c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-65-18","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":65,"verse":18,"english":"And the greatest piety of the Vaiśyas and Śūdras at that time consisted of serving the Brāhmaṇas and Ksatriyas and specially for the Śūdras the highest religion was to serve people of all Varnas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.697,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-74-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7065018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8b245ca4503bc714f68d15b22524e02b756a6c3610a3eeab00b3dcb451b78dbb","compact":"048e2c46c99a47168a5c93857fddc4f04a51d33b5adf4148e21cfac225d6ab2e","nasal":"048e2c46c99a47168a5c93857fddc4f04a51d33b5adf4148e21cfac225d6ab2e"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-65-19","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":65,"verse":19,"english":"And the second foot of impiety being ushered into the world the Dvāpara age set in.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-74-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7065019","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0af335c701b2f00db26db0485ad62409e24b73a7acea1da05183c520a181df4f","compact":"b272b2d881d24ba3f10c52c6665b83d694e7584bf67880c85eacf3e7a20623a8","nasal":"b272b2d881d24ba3f10c52c6665b83d694e7584bf67880c85eacf3e7a20623a8"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-65-20","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":65,"verse":20,"english":"O foremost of men, during this age two legs of piety being cut off, impiety and untruth multiplies.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-74-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7065020","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8f0aa9169973f6dfe9d08a7cdb6d978eb57dea381b8d4aaa149a1e1cba287cb7","compact":"cb674ce5fe76886fb72423efd485bce4c8ca94c06f3de2bfbbafd937ee675a24","nasal":"e8b7bf577e94c679a714621bfcfa53f67a036b13d5c7bb02e8b9f5c9922f0fc4"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-65-21","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":65,"verse":21,"english":"And in Yuga named Dvāpara the Vaisyas engaged in devout penances. In this wise in three ages the three Varnas gradually engaged in ascetic performances.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.369,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-74-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7065021","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"43831b34606f37c28c3515c896d4370e28c5d8af6151410a39fb5f45c556caf3","compact":"feb65a4bde50f4b22e98f96a121bdb09de79617a3f22870a9e5b8e18bc6df474","nasal":"b9aea95f500fba537005246ad2b5c1099c1c26869b156d95cc68894ec5c75363"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-65-22","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":65,"verse":22,"english":"O foremost of men, the degraded caste, the Śūdras, during your rege me, have engaged in austere penances. And in the Kali Yuga asceticism shall be established in the Sūdras.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.726,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-74-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7065022","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9b8e48cdcda961da355515bb36fbf5553fa49664b389cd3294b634a2197ea679","compact":"b288670e214e1178785a162e3c35a00972b2d6128941e71615c92fee01fd7ff3","nasal":"b288670e214e1178785a162e3c35a00972b2d6128941e71615c92fee01fd7ff3"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-65-23","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":65,"verse":23,"english":"O king, even in Davāpara, devout penances for Śūdras were considered as impiety, what to speak of the Tretāage. O king, one Śūdras, under the influence of vicious understanding, has begun devout penances within your kingdom. And for that reason this boy has met with death.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.634,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-74-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7065023","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. 